    "description": "Whether formal international legal accountability proceedings are initiated — at the ICC, ICJ, or through UN Special Rapporteur mechanisms — for alleged war crimes, crimes against humanity, or serious violations of international humanitarian law. Relevant triggers: deliberate infrastructure attacks, disproportionate civilian casualties, use of certain weapons categories, siege-like denial of aid. The US is not an ICC signatory but ICC jurisdiction could apply over Iranian territory and nationals of signatory states. The ICJ could receive inter-state applications (Iran vs. USA, as in 1980 hostages case). Post-2023 Gaza precedent has significantly lowered the political threshold for initiating ICC and ICJ proceedings against Western states. Russia-China vetoes would block UNSC referral but ICC Prosecutor has proprio motu authority. Domestic Congressional and allied-nation judicial proceedings provide additional vectors.",
